; HTTP as both ends of a call speak it: heads, bodies by every framing and
; the writer, read and written strictly; WebSockets, and the JSON they carry;
; and what a line is logged with and a fiber runs under. Its own library
; rather than modules of `spindle`, because the server and `spindle_client`
; both speak it and must speak it one way, and the client depends on it
; alone -- a program that calls other servers links no framework. It holds
; no socket and no policy: every limit it applies is one it is given.

(library
 (name spindle_http)
 (public_name spindle.http)
 (private_modules frame grammar calendar context)
 (libraries
  eio
  mtime
  logs
  wiretype
  digestif
  base64
  angstrom
  ipaddr
  threads.posix))
